{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rebel-vaporous-martin","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The completion-verifier close gate FAILS OPEN on an LLM provider error: the ticket closes with no attestation\n\nA close whose completion verifier dies mid-run **succeeds anyway**, leaving the ticket `closed`\nwith no `completion-verifier` attestation. The same gate FAILS CLOSED when the provider package\nis merely absent. Two failure modes of one dependency, opposite outcomes, and the one that lets\nwork through unverified is the one that fires when the provider is reachable but unhappy.\n\n## Observed\n\nClosing epic `e369-a449-4773-48fb`:\n\n    rebar.llm.errors.LLMUnavailableError: the LLM provider call failed: status_code: 400,\n    model_name: us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0,\n    'The maximum tokens you requested exceeds the model limit of 64000.\n     Try again with a maximum tokens value that is lower than 64000.' (ValidationException)\n\n    ...and then:  UNBLOCKED: none          exit code 0\n\nResult:\n\n    rebar show e369-a449-4773-48fb  ->  status: closed\n    attestation kinds present:          ['plan-review']\n    completion-verifier:                ABSENT\n\n## Contrast — the same gate fails CLOSED for a neighbouring cause\n\nEarlier in the same session, with the bedrock provider package not installed, three closes were\ncorrectly REFUSED:\n\n    Error: cannot close 1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda: completion verification could not run\n    (... a bedrock model/provider is configured but the optional bedrock provider package is not\n    installed ...). Override with --force-close=\"<reason>\".\n\nSo the gate KNOWS how to refuse. A missing package refuses; a 400 from the provider does not.\n\n## Why this is worse than a flaky gate\n\nThe whole point of the completion verifier is that a human or agent cannot mark work done without\nan independent check. A gate that disappears exactly when the provider is degraded is a gate that\nis absent precisely when nobody is watching closely — and it leaves NO signal on the ticket. The\nticket reads `closed`; only the absent attestation and a stack trace scrolled past in the terminal\ndistinguish it from a verified close.\n\nThis is the same silent-success shape epic e369 spent its life removing from the Jira bridge, now\nin the gate that is supposed to certify that removal.\n\n## Two defects, and they are separable\n\n1. **Fail-open on provider error.** `LLMUnavailableError` during completion verification must\n   refuse the close, exactly as the missing-package path does, and say so.\n2. **The 400 itself.** A `max_tokens` above 64000 is requested against\n   `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0`, whose ceiling is 64000. Bedrock rejects it\n   outright, so the trivial-class model is unusable for this step as configured. Likely fallout\n   from defaulting local dev to Bedrock — the direct-Anthropic path evidently tolerated the same\n   request.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] a completion verifier that raises `LLMUnavailableError` REFUSES the close, with the same\n      remedy text and `--force-close` escape hatch the missing-package path already prints\n- [ ] a test pins the refusal, driving the verifier to raise rather than asserting on a mock's\n      call count\n- [ ] the `max_tokens` request is clamped to the configured model's ceiling, or the step is not\n      routed to a model whose ceiling it exceeds\n- [ ] epic e369's close is re-verified once the gate works, or its close is explicitly accepted\n      without a completion attestation and that decision is recorded on the ticket","id":"1019-e1e9-5117-4795","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion-verifier close gate fails OPEN on an LLM provider error: the ticket closes with no attestation"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785827831798139001,"uuid":"a10a5108-bdc9-4626-b4ad-7db8ee87df15"}